{"archetypes":[{"name":"sentinel-boundary","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The core change relaxes a strict whole-content match to a first-non-empty-line match; subtle boundary cases around CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE, the JSON sentinel, and trimmed_nonblank_content interaction deserve close scrutiny.","prompt_body":"Examine the two sentinel-check blocks in scripts/validate-research-output.sh. Verify that CURSOR_EMPTY_RESPONSE is still matched against the full TRIMMED content and not against FIRST_LINE. Check that the awk one-liner `NF { print; exit }` correctly extracts the first non-empty line from TRIMMED (which is already through trimmed_nonblank_content) — confirm there is no double-stripping or off-by-one when TRIMMED itself starts with a blank line. Confirm that the JSON no-findings sentinel path (`jq -e`) now receives FIRST_LINE and that a file whose first non-empty line is the JSON sentinel but has trailing prose will correctly exit 0 in both validation-mode and structured-reviewer-mode. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-coverage","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Cases 60-63 are the only regression tests for the new behavior; verifying their fixture content, expected exit codes, and mode flags are internally consistent with the implementation is essential.","prompt_body":"Review cases 60-63 in scripts/test-validate-research-output.sh. Confirm each fixture string (constructed via printf) matches the documented scenario in the comment: sentinel on first line vs. not-first-line, and the correct --validation-mode vs. --structured-reviewer-mode flag. Check that case 61 correctly expects exit 2 (not exit 5) because the body falls through to the word-count gate in validation-mode, and that case 63 correctly expects exit 5 (not exit 2) because structured-reviewer-mode bypasses word-count and hits the no-valid-records path. Verify that the case-count header comments at the top of the test file are updated consistently with the new cases. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
